WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.703
-My next guest is a fantastic
actor who you know from

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.805
films like "Crazy Rich Asians"
and "The Gentlemen."

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.275
His latest movie, "Monsoon,"
is available in virtual cinemas

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.745
and on demand on your favorite
streaming platform.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.713
Here is Henry Golding, everyone.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.815
-Hey!
-Oh, come on!

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.783
It is so great to see you.
-What's up, Jimmy?

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:19.952
-Ah! Thank you so much for
coming on the show.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.554
You look great, buddy.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.389
Before we start the interview,
I just want to say,

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:26.559
I wish you were in person so I
can say congratulations,

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.395
because you and your wife, Liv,
are expecting a baby!

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:32.298
-We are! Our first. Man!

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.201
I made the most out
of quarantine, you know?

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.536
-Yes!
-We got there.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:37.971
-That's great!

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.574
-It's literally the only time
that we've spent longer than

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.410
two or three months together
without traveling.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.512
So, I think a lot of people
were like,

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.881
"This is the time you've got to
concentrate on family.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.517
This is the time where
you reconnect."

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.285
And we just made the most of it.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.253
We're so excited.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:57.057
-We need good news these days.
This is such good news.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.858
Honestly, you're gonna be
the best dad.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.759
Congrats on that.
-Oh, I appreciate it.

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:02.295
-Before we talk about your
movie, "Monsoon,"

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.263
I want to ask you about another
movie you're starring in,

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.398
"Snake Eyes."

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.866
It comes out next year.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:11.604
-Snake Eyes -- this is from --
Anyone who knows "G.I. Joe."

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.505
I was into "G.I. Joe"
growing up.

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:14.774
Probably a little bit too late.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.309
I think my parents
had to be like,

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.710
"Okay, you're too old for this."

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.546
But I was watching every day
after school and into it,

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:21.648
into the cartoons.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.016
I had all the action figures.
-Damn!

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.150
-And now -- Wait.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.587
So, is this like
an origin story?

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:31.224
-So, this is -- Yeah, it's
Snake Eyes' "G.I. Joe" origins.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.426
We start all the way from
the beginning

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:37.496
to get to the core of
who this guy is.

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:38.931
It's super-exciting.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:41.534
-This is a giant, giant, giant
action movie.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.802
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.737
-I mean, was it "Gentlemen"
that got you into the --

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:48.875
everyone was like,
"Oh, he can do action great"?

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.410
-They definitely went out on
a whim for me.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.013
Like, they had no idea
I could achieve any of this.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.181
-Did you know that
you could achieve it?

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.216
-Luckily, like,
my movement's pretty good.

00:01:57.216 --> 00:02:01.220
I've been boxing for a little
while and a bit of Muay Thai.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.755
But it put me through my paces.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:06.158
We had like four hours of
choreography every single day.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:09.229
We had two hours of script work,
then like an hour of P.T.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.599
For literally 2 1/2 months,
I could not sit on the toilet

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.302
and I could not -- Well, and if
I made my way to the toilet,

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.437
I couldn't get up
from the toilet.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.704
Literally,
my legs were in ruins.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:19.972
-Really?

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:23.009
-But it was worth it,
because I became a weapon.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.510
I'm not going to lie.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.880
You actually brought us footage
of you rehearsing

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.948
some of your fight scenes

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.016
and you cleared it
with Paramount,

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.016
so thank you for doing this.

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.385
-I know.
This is a world exclusive.

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:35.855
Nobody has seen anything,
apart from a photo from behind.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.324
-Here's Henry Golding training
for "Snake Eyes."

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.492
Look at this.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:49.335
-Hey!
-Oh!

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.737
Yeah! Come on, dude!
-Yeah!

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:55.908
-Oh, my gosh! Oh!
And face! Yes!

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:58.311
Oh, my gosh!
-You've got to do the look-away.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.712
You have to do the look-away.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.314
If you look at the fallen bodies
on the floor, it's not cool.

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:04.450
You've just got to, like...
-Of course.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.385
You walk away from the explosion
like it didn't happen.

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:07.386
-Exactly!
-It's right behind you.

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:08.887
It's over.

00:03:08.887 --> 00:03:12.324
That was -- I mean, Look at the
work that just went into that.

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:14.427
That's one scene in the movie.
-I know.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.295
A little different from
Nick young of

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:17.529
"Crazy Rich Asians."

00:03:17.529 --> 00:03:19.865
So I'm super-excited
for everybody to see this.

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.366
Sadly, you know,
with everything going on,

00:03:21.366 --> 00:03:25.405
we had to move it from
this October to next October,

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.172
but it's going to be great.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:31.110
-Next October, "Snake Eyes" will
be in theaters October 2021.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.380
Thanks for brings that footage.
I'm so psyched about that.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.882
Let's talk about "Monsoon."

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.350
It is out now.
-Hey!

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.386
Can you tell everyone
what it's about?

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:44.189
-Yeah. It's about a young man
who's Vietnamese

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:47.993
but grew up in the U.K.,
much kind of like my story

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.862
of being Malaysian and
growing up in the U.K.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.963
-Yeah.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:53.833
-He finally finds
his way back to Vietnam.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.435
And a lot of time when you go
back to your motherland,

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:57.870
you kind of feel
this sense of like,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.606
"Oh, I'm going to feel
a connection.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.442
I'm going to be home."

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:05.745
But a lot of the time
and more often than not,

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.913
there's a sense of alienation.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.048
You don't speak the language.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.083
You don't understand
the culture.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:14.620
So what would or should
feel like coming home

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.056
feels very, very weird.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.626
So, it's a young man
delving into his past,

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:22.996
his history, and trying to find
kind of his true identity.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:27.633
-Wow! I know that before movies,
didn't you host a travel show?

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:30.603
-That's right, yeah.
-I remember you saying that.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.371
Did you ever try to connect to
your roots or find out,

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.472
you know, where exactly --

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:35.208
-You know what
the greatest thing was?

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:38.544
When I was doing all the
journalism for the travel shows,

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:42.248
I actually brought my camera
and I sat my parents down,

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:46.418
and, through the filter of
a camera, they just open up,

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:47.920
because, like,
talking to face-to-face is

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.221
so difficult sometimes.

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:52.825
So when you kind of make it
into an interview,

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.527
something else in their brain
kind of triggers,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.396
and they're like,
"Oh, I better tell the truth" or

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.764
"I better tell, like,
the entire story,

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.033
not the convenient truth."

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.466
-Wow!

00:05:01.466 --> 00:05:04.236
-So, I did that and I have this,
like, beautiful footage

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.705
of my parents letting me know --
like, telling me

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:09.708
how they met,
what their lives were before.

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:12.211
And it's so difficult to
get that out of them sometimes,

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.512
you know?

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.814
-You know who's really going to
benefit from this?

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:18.450
Is baby. It's the best.
-Yes.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.620
-That's so true.
-Oh, buddy, that's so cool.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.488
-I'm going to store
this interview.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.623
-Yeah! This is the opener.
-Play it in the crib.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:26.492
-Yeah.
Just add the name in later.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:31.964
Like..."Enjoy the clip of your
dad talking to his parents."

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.400
You can add that in post.
You put that in post.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.670
I want to show everyone a clip
of Henry Golding in "Monsoon."

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.871
Take a look at this.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.007
-I mean, there are some parts
that remind me of

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:44.377
the Vietnam I grew up in,
mainly the poorer parts,

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:47.213
like that street behind
the hospital.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:49.715
-When we first met, you said it
was your first time here.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:52.251
-Did I?

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.520
-Yeah. You did.

00:05:56.488 --> 00:05:59.025
-I lied.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.259
Sorry.

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:02.795
-Why?

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:06.666
-Keep it simple.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.708
-You just can't get enough
of me, can you?

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.944
I have that effect.
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:20.312
-Henry Golding, everybody.

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:23.649
"Monsoon" is available in
virtual cinemas and on demand

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.218
on your favorite
streaming platform.

